{title: Let Us Start Rebuilding}
{subtitle: Nehemiah 2:17–20; 4:1–17; 6:15–16}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [B] | [F#] | [C#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D#m]The walls were down, the gates were [B]burned
The city lay in [F#]shame [C#]
[D#m]Nehemiah rode by [B]moonlight
And he came back with a [F#]flame [C#]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Come, let us re[B]build the wall of Jeru[F#]salem
Let us [C#]start rebuilding
[D#m]The God of heaven will [B]give us success
Let us [F#]start rebuild[C#]ing [D#m]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Sanballat laughed and Tobiah [B]sneered
What is this you are [F#]doing [C#]
[D#m]But they set their hands to the [B]good work
And they kept on with [F#]the build[C#]ing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Come, let us re[B]build the wall of Jeru[F#]salem
Let us [C#]start rebuilding
[D#m]The God of heaven will [B]give us success
Let us [F#]start rebuild[C#]ing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]A trowel in one hand, a sword in the oth[D#m]er
Sister by sister and brother by brother
[F#]In fif-ty-two days the wall was fin[C#]ished
For this work had been accom[D#m]plished by our [B]God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Let us start [F#]rebuild[C#]ing [D#m][B]
Let us start [F#]rebuild[C#]ing
{end_of_verse}

